«
@@ ============================================================
@@ LOPFix — position from two or more lines of position, by least squares on
@@ their intercepts and azimuths from an assumed position.
@@ 
@@ Input : φ λ lines — assumed latitude and longitude, and a list of { Zn a }:
@@         true azimuth and intercept, positive toward the body. Plain numbers are
@@         degrees and nautical miles; units are accepted.
@@ Output: φ λ — the position. For intercepts above about 30 NM, repeat from there.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ ============================================================

  → lns
  «
    IF lns SIZE 2 < THEN "A fix needs at least two lines" DOERR END
    2 →LIST « →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_° CONVERT UVAL END » MAP LIST→ DROP
    'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
    RAD NoAngleUnits
    Ⓒπ →Num 180 / 0 0 0 0 0
    → lat lon amode aunits rdn caa cab cbb cdd cee
    «
      1 lns SIZE FOR kk
        lns kk GET 1 GET →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_° CONVERT UVAL END rdn *
        lns kk GET 2 GET IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_nmi CONVERT UVAL END →Num
        → zaz itc
        «
          'caa+COS(zaz)²' EVAL 'caa' STO
          'cab+COS(zaz)*SIN(zaz)' EVAL 'cab' STO
          'cbb+SIN(zaz)²' EVAL 'cbb' STO
          'cdd+itc*COS(zaz)' EVAL 'cdd' STO
          'cee+itc*SIN(zaz)' EVAL 'cee' STO
        »
      NEXT
      'caa*cbb-cab²' EVAL
      → dtr
      «
        IF dtr ABS 1E-9 < THEN
          0 0 1
        ELSE
          'lat+(cbb*cdd-cab*cee)/dtr/60' EVAL 1_° *
          'lon+(caa*cee-cab*cdd)/(dtr*COS(lat*rdn))/60' EVAL 1_° *
          0
        END
      »
      amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
    »
    → phf lmf bad
    «
      IF bad THEN "The lines are parallel" DOERR END
      phf lmf
    »
  »
»
